+# Codepod port notes
+
+This curl build targets Codepod's wasm guest ABI. It deliberately keeps curl
+as a single-process, in-sandbox executable.
+
+Unsupported process features:
+
+- `fork()` and `vfork()` are disabled at configure time with
+  `ac_cv_func_fork=no` and `ac_cv_func_vfork=no`.
+- The threaded resolver is disabled with `--disable-threaded-resolver`.
+- External helper execution is not part of this port. Features that would
+  require launching host programs must be represented as explicit Codepod ABI
+  calls instead.
+
+Networking is selected at runtime:
+
+- `auto` uses the port default.
+- `fetch` routes HTTP through Codepod's `host_network_fetch` ABI.
+- `socket` routes through the POSIX socket compatibility layer.
+
+The wasm may still contain libc documentation strings mentioning process
+functions, but the curl port must not depend on `fork()` or `vfork()` imports.
